        // Terrazzo
        terrazzo_category: "Premium Decorative",
        terrazzo_title: "Terrazzo Floor Systems",
        terrazzo_meta: "Timeless Aggregate Beauty",
        terrazzo_lead: "Marble, glass, or stone aggregates suspended in cement or epoxy matrix \u2014 then ground and polished to reveal depth and character. A floor with soul that can last generations.",
        terrazzo_h2_where: "Where Terrazzo Shines",
        terrazzo_p_where: "Terrazzo has been a symbol of elegance and durability for centuries. Today, it continues to be the flooring choice for spaces where design impact and longevity are paramount.",
        terrazzo_app1_title: "Airports & Transit",
        terrazzo_app1_desc: "Million-footfall durability. Wayfinding patterns, logos, and brand integration. Low lifetime cost.",
        terrazzo_app2_title: "Luxury Retail",
        terrazzo_app2_desc: "Statement floors that elevate brand experience. Custom aggregate selections and patterns.",
        terrazzo_app3_title: "Hotels & Lobbies",
        terrazzo_app3_desc: "Grand entrance statements. Combines durability with visual impact. Heritage or contemporary.",
        terrazzo_app4_title: "Healthcare",
        terrazzo_app4_desc: "Seamless, hygienic, easy to clean. Infection control compliant. Lifetime durability reduces replacement costs.",
        terrazzo_h2_substrate: "Substrate Preparation",
        terrazzo_p_substrate: "Terrazzo is a permanent installation requiring proper structural support. Substrate preparation varies by system type but is critical for long-term performance.",
        terrazzo_sub1: "<strong>Cement terrazzo (traditional)</strong> \u2014 Requires sand-cement bed over waterproof membrane. Total buildup 25-50mm",
        terrazzo_sub2: "<strong>Epoxy terrazzo (thin-set)</strong> \u2014 Applied directly to prepared concrete. 10-12mm total thickness",
        terrazzo_sub3: "<strong>Divider strips</strong> \u2014 Brass, zinc, or plastic strips control cracking and create design patterns",
        terrazzo_sub4: "<strong>Expansion joints</strong> \u2014 Must align with structural joints. Filled with flexible sealant",
        terrazzo_sub5: "<strong>Moisture control</strong> \u2014 Critical for epoxy systems. Vapor barrier or mitigation required if RH >75%",
        terrazzo_h2_process: "The Terrazzo Process",
        terrazzo_p_process: "Every terrazzo installation follows a time-tested process that transforms raw materials into enduring works of art.",
        terrazzo_layer1_title: "Pour & Place",
        terrazzo_layer1_desc: "Matrix (cement or epoxy) mixed with selected aggregates, poured between divider strips, and spread to specified depth. Aggregates hand-seeded for density.",
        terrazzo_layer2_title: "Grinding",
        terrazzo_layer2_desc: "Progressive grinding with diamond-segment machines exposes aggregate faces. Multiple passes from coarse (40 grit) to fine (200+ grit) create smooth surface.",
        terrazzo_layer3_title: "Grouting & Polishing",
        terrazzo_layer3_desc: "Pinholes filled with matching grout, then polished to final sheen. Penetrating sealer protects without altering appearance.",
        terrazzo_h2_aggregates: "Aggregate Options",
        terrazzo_p_aggregates: "The beauty of terrazzo lies in its endless design possibilities through aggregate selection:",
        terrazzo_var1_title: "Marble Chips",
        terrazzo_var1_desc: "Classic terrazzo aggregate. Sizes from 0 (fine) to 8 (large). Natural color variations.",
        terrazzo_var2_title: "Glass",
        terrazzo_var2_desc: "Recycled or virgin glass in unlimited colors. Reflective sparkle, sustainable option.",
        terrazzo_var3_title: "Mother of Pearl",
        terrazzo_var3_desc: "Crushed shell for iridescent effect. Luxury residential and hospitality applications.",
        terrazzo_var4_title: "Mixed / Custom",
        terrazzo_var4_desc: "Combine aggregates for unique effects. Seashells, metal, mirror \u2014 possibilities endless.",
        terrazzo_h2_advantages: "Key Advantages",
        terrazzo_adv1: "<strong>Exceptional Longevity</strong> \u2014 50+ year service life. Many terrazzo floors installed in the 1920s still perform today.",
        terrazzo_adv2: "<strong>Design Freedom</strong> \u2014 Unlimited colors, patterns, logos, and inlays. True custom design capability.",
        terrazzo_adv3: "<strong>Low Lifecycle Cost</strong> \u2014 Higher upfront cost offset by decades of service. Restorable, not replaceable.",
        terrazzo_adv4: "<strong>Sustainable</strong> \u2014 Recycled glass and post-consumer aggregates. VOC-free cement systems. LEED credits.",
        terrazzo_adv5: "<strong>Seamless & Hygienic</strong> \u2014 No grout lines. Divider strips are integral. Easy to clean and maintain.",
        terrazzo_adv6: "<strong>Restorable</strong> \u2014 Can be reground and repolished to original condition. Floor that improves with age.",
        terrazzo_h2_maintenance: "Maintenance Protocol",
        terrazzo_p_maintenance: "Terrazzo is remarkably low-maintenance. The grinding and polishing process creates a dense, closed surface that resists staining and wear.",
        terrazzo_maint_daily: "Dust mop to remove abrasive particles. Damp mop high-traffic areas as needed.",
        terrazzo_maint_weekly: "Wet mop with neutral pH cleaner. Auto-scrubber for large areas.",
        terrazzo_maint_annually: "Professional diamond honing of high-traffic areas. Reapply penetrating sealer.",
        terrazzo_maint_cycle: "Every 10-20 Years",
        terrazzo_maint_cycle_desc: "Full restoration grinding and polishing as needed to restore original appearance.",
        terrazzo_cta_title: "Ready for Your Terrazzo Project?",
        terrazzo_cta_text: "Our design team will help you create a custom terrazzo floor that will last generations.",
        terrazzo_specs_title: "Technical Specifications",
        terrazzo_spec_thickness: "System Thickness",
